From 2abe4632d793314d3d5f28c19583fb76019f5ce4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Hutterer <peter.hutterer@who-t.net>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 17:16:49 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] glx: validate dataBytes against cmdlen in RenderLarge
 first request

__glXDisp_RenderLarge() allocates the large command buffer based on
cmdlen (from hdr->length, the total command size embedded in the
payload), but copies dataBytes (from req->dataBytes, the payload size
of the current sub-request) into it. The existing length check only
validates that the X11 request length is consistent with dataBytes,
not that dataBytes fits within the cmdlen-sized buffer.

A malicious client can set hdr->length to a small value (e.g. 12 bytes)
while sending a large dataBytes (up to ~256KB or more with
BIG-REQUESTS), causing the memcpy to overflow the cmdlen-sized buffer.

Add a check that dataBytes <= cmdlen before the buffer allocation and
copy on the first request.

This vulnerability was discovered by:
  Anonymous working with TrendAI Zero Day Initiative

ZDI-CAN-31833

CVE-2026-93517

Signed-off-by: Peter Hutterer <peter.hutterer@who-t.net>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-4-6
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/xserver/-/merge_requests/2341>
---
 glx/glxcmds.c             |  3 ++
 test/pyxtest/proto/glx.py | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++
 test/pyxtest/test_glx.py  | 94 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 147 insertions(+)

diff --git a/glx/glxcmds.c b/glx/glxcmds.c
index 58ef861f5..39b187fd9 100644
--- a/glx/glxcmds.c
+++ b/glx/glxcmds.c
@@ -2187,6 +2187,9 @@ __glXDisp_RenderLarge(__GLXclientState * cl, GLbyte * pc)
             return BadLength;
         }
 
+        if (dataBytes > cmdlen)
+            return BadLength;
+
         /*
          ** Make enough space in the buffer, then copy the entire request.
          */
